# Keep line endings stable across platforms.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true on Windows, a checkout rewrites files to CRLF. For
# most sources that is harmless, but the migration runner records a checksum of
# each .sql file, so a checkout alone made it refuse to run — reporting that an
# applied migration had been modified when nobody had touched it. Shell scripts
# are pinned for the older reason: CRLF breaks the shebang on Linux.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf

# Never normalise binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jks   binary
*.keystore binary
